  "files": [
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Temperature Converter</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\" aria-labelledby=\"title\">\n    <h1 id=\"title\">Pixel Temp Converter</h1>\n    <p class=\"hint\">C to F: x*9/5+32 &nbsp;|&nbsp; F to C: (x-32)*5/9</p>\n\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <label for=\"temperature\">Temperature</label>\n      <input id=\"temperature\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" placeholder=\"e.g. 100\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <label for=\"direction\">Direction</label>\n      <select id=\"direction\">\n        <option value=\"c-to-f\">Celsius &rarr; Fahrenheit</option>\n        <option value=\"f-to-c\">Fahrenheit &rarr; Celsius</option>\n      </select>\n    </div>\n\n    <button id=\"convert\" type=\"button\">Convert</button>\n\n    <div class=\"output\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <span class=\"output-label\">Result</span>\n      <output id=\"result\">--</output>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
      "description": "Main HTML page with labeled controls and required IDs."
    },
    {
      "path": "style.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1a1c2c;\n  --panel: #f4f4f4;\n  --ink: #1a1c2c;\n  --accent: #ffcd75;\n  --accent-dark: #e0a800;\n  --muted: #5d6070;\n  --border: 4px solid var(--ink);\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  padding: 16px;\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  background-image:\n    linear-gradient(45deg, #22243a 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, #22243a 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 75%, #22243a 75%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 75%, #22243a 75%);\n  background-size: 24px 24px;\n  background-position: 0 0, 0 12px, 12px -12px, -12px 0;\n  font-family: ui-monospace, \"Cascadia Code\", \"Courier New\", monospace;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--ink);\n}\n\n.card {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 420px;\n  background: var(--panel);\n  border: var(--border);\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--accent-dark);\n  padding: 24px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 1.35rem;\n  line-height: 1.3;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\n\n.hint {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.field {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 6px;\n}\n\nlabel {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n}\n\ninput, select, button {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  padding: 10px 12px;\n  border: 3px solid var(--ink);\n  border-radius: 0;\n  background: #fff;\n  color: var(--ink);\n  transition: transform 0.05s, box-shadow 0.05s;\n}\n\ninput:hover, select:hover {\n  background: #fffbe8;\n}\n\ninput:focus-visible, select:focus-visible, button:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--accent-dark);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  cursor: pointer;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink);\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #ffd98f;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: translate(4px, 4px);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--ink);\n}\n\n.output {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: baseline;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  gap: 12px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  border: 3px dashed var(--ink);\n  background: #fff;\n}\n\n.output-label {\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n\n#result {\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  word-break: break-all;\n  text-align: right;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  .card { padding: 16px; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--accent-dark); }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.15rem; }\n  #result { font-size: 1.35rem; }\n}\n",
      "description": "Pixel-themed responsive stylesheet."
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  var input = document.getElementById(\"temperature\");\n  var direction = document.getElementById(\"direction\");\n  var button = document.getElementById(\"convert\");\n  var result = document.getElementById(\"result\");\n\n  function convert() {\n    var raw = input.value.trim();\n    var value = raw === \"\" ? NaN : Number(raw);\n\n    if (!isFinite(value)) {\n      result.textContent = \"Error\";\n      return;\n    }\n\n    var converted = direction.value === \"c-to-f\"\n      ? value * 9 / 5 + 32\n      : (value - 32) * 5 / 9;\n\n    result.textContent = converted.toFixed(2);\n  }\n\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", convert);\n\n  input.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (event) {\n    if (event.key === \"Enter\") {\n      event.preventDefault();\n      convert();\n    }\n  });\n})();\n",
      "description": "Conversion logic and validation."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Temperature Converter\n\nAn offline, pixel-styled temperature converter built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No packages, network requests, or storage.\n\n## Usage\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser.\n\n1. Enter a numeric temperature in the **Temperature** field.\n2. Choose a direction:\n   - **Celsius → Fahrenheit**: `x * 9 / 5 + 32`\n   - **Fahrenheit → Celsius**: `(x - 32) * 5 / 9`\n3. Click **Convert** (or press Enter in the input).\n\nThe result appears with exactly two decimals and no unit. Empty, non-numeric, or non-finite input shows `Error`.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — markup and labeled controls\n- `style.css` — pixel theme and responsive layout\n- `script.js` — conversion logic and validation\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- All controls have associated labels.\n- Full keyboard support with visible focus states.\n- Result area uses `aria-live` for announcements.\n",
      "description": "Project documentation."
    }
  ]
}